own","annotare","ahn-noh-TAH-reh"],["to listen","ascoltare","ah-skol-TAH-reh"],["to read aloud","leggere ad alta voce","LEHD-jeh-reh ahd AHL-tah VOH-cheh"],["to think","pensare","pehn-SAH-reh"],["to count","contare","kon-TAH-reh"],["to spell","sillabare","seel-lah-BAH-reh"],["to translate","tradurre","trah-DOOR-reh"],["to graduate","laurearsi","low-reh-AR-see"]]}],"grammar":[{"id":"pronouns","title":"Pronouns","text":["Italian drops subject pronouns most of the time, because the verb ending shows who is speaking."],"rows":[["I","io","EE-oh"],["you (informal)","tu","too"],["he / she","lui / lei","LOO-ee / lay"],["we","noi","noy"],["you all","voi","voy"],["they","loro","LOH-roh"],["you (formal)","Lei","lay"]],"ex":[["I am a student","io sono studente","EE-oh SOH-noh stoo-DEHN-teh"],["you are tall","tu sei alto","too say AHL-toh"],["she is my sister","lei è mia sorella","lay eh MEE-ah soh-REHL-lah"],["we are friends","noi siamo amici","noy SYAH-moh ah-MEE-chee"],["they are teachers","loro sono insegnanti","LOH-roh SOH-noh een-sehn-YAHN-tee"]]},{"id":"singular-and-plural","title":"Singular and plural","text":["Masculine -o → -i. Feminine -a → -e. Words in -e → -i. The article changes too: il → i, la → le, lo → gli."],"rows":[["-o to -i (m)","il libro → i libri","ee LEE-bree"],["-a to -e (f)","la casa → le case","leh KAH-zeh"],["-e to -i","il cane → i cani","ee KAH-nee"],["lo to gli","lo studente → gli studenti","lyee stoo-DEHN-tee"]],"ex":[["one book, two books","un libro, due libri","oon LEE-broh DOO-eh LEE-bree"],["one house, houses","una casa, le case","OO-nah KAH-zah leh KAH-zeh"],["one dog, dogs","un cane, i cani","oon KAH-neh ee KAH-nee"],["one student, students","uno studente, gli studenti","OO-noh stoo-DEHN-teh lyee stoo-DEHN-tee"],["one friend (f), friends","un'amica, le amiche","oon-ah-MEE-kah leh ah-MEE-keh"]]},{"id":"essere-to-be","title":"Essere: to be","text":[],"rows":[["I am","io sono","EE-oh SOH-noh"],["you are","tu sei","too SAY"],["he / she is","lui / lei è","LOO-ee / lay EH"],["we are","noi siamo","noy SYAH-moh"],["you all are","voi siete","voy SYEH-teh"],["they are","loro sono","LOH-roh SOH-noh"]],"ex":[["I am English","sono inglese","SOH-noh een-GLEH-zeh"],["he is a doctor","è medico","eh MEH-dee-koh"],["we are tired","siamo stanchi","SYAH-moh STAHN-kee"],["are you from Rome?","sei di Roma?","say dee ROH-mah"],["they are at home","sono a casa","SOH-noh ah KAH-zah"]]},{"id":"avere-to-have","title":"Avere: to have","text":["Avere is also used for age and feelings: ho sedici anni, ho fame, ho sete."],"rows":[["I have","io ho","oh"],["you have","tu hai","eye"],["he / she has","lui / lei ha","ah"],["we have","noi abbiamo","ahb-BYAH-moh"],["you all have","voi avete","ah-VEH-teh"],["they have","loro hanno","AHN-noh"]],"ex":[["I have a brother","ho un fratello","oh oon frah-TEHL-loh"],["she has two cats","ha due gatti","ah DOO-eh GAHT-tee"],["we have time","abbiamo tempo","ahb-BYAH-moh TEHM-poh"],["I am hungry","ho fame","oh FAH-meh"],["they have a car","hanno una macchina","AHN-noh OO-nah MAHK-kee-nah"]]},{"id":"regular-verbs-present-tense","title":"Regular verbs (present tense)","text":["Three families: -are, -ere, -ire. Drop the ending, add the new one. Parlare (to speak):"],"rows":[["io","parlo","PAR-loh"],["tu","parli","PAR-lee"],["lui / lei","parla","PAR-lah"],["noi","parliamo","par-LYAH-moh"],["voi","parlate","par-LAH-teh"],["loro","parlano","PAR-lah-noh"]],"ex":[["I speak English","parlo inglese","PAR-loh een-GLEH-zeh"],["you eat a lot","mangi molto","MAHN-jee MOHL-toh"],["she lives in Rome","abita a Roma","AH-bee-tah ah ROH-mah"],["we work every day","lavoriamo ogni giorno","lah-voh-RYAH-moh OHN-yee JOR-noh"],["they drink water","bevono acqua","BEH-voh-noh AHK-kwah"]]},{"id":"andare-to-go","title":"Andare: to go","text":["Going to do something soon: andare + a + infinitive. Vado a mangiare = I am going to eat."],"rows":[["I go","io vado","VAH-doh"],["you go","tu vai","vy"],["he / she goes","lui / lei va","vah"],["we go","noi andiamo","ahn-DYAH-moh"],["you all go","voi andate","ahn-DAH-teh"],["they go","loro vanno","VAHN-noh"]],"ex":[["I am going to school","vado a scuola","VAH-doh ah SKWOH-lah"],["where are you going?","dove vai?","DOH-veh vy"],["we are going to eat","andiamo a mangiare","ahn-DYAH-moh ah mahn-JAH-reh"],["she is going to travel","va a viaggiare","vah ah vyahd-JAH-reh"],["let's go!","andiamo!","ahn-DYAH-moh"]]},{"id":"basic-sentences","title":"Basic sentences","text":["Order: subject, verb, rest. Adjectives usually come after the noun and agree with it. You can drop the subject."],"rows":[["subject + verb + rest","Mangio il pane.","MAHN-joh eel PAH-neh"],["adjective after noun","una casa grande","OO-nah KAH-zah GRAHN-deh"],["add time or place at the end","Lavoro qui oggi.","lah-VOH-roh kwee OHD-jee"]],"ex":[["I eat bread","mangio il pane","MAHN-joh eel PAH-neh"],["Maria reads a book","Maria legge un libro","mah-REE-ah LEJ-jeh oon LEE-broh"],["we live in a big house","abitiamo in una casa grande","ah-bee-TYAH-moh een OO-nah KAH-zah GRAHN-deh"],["he works here today","lavora qui oggi","lah-VOH-rah kwee OHD-jee"],["the dog is black","il cane è nero","eel KAH-neh eh NEH-roh"]]},{"id":"negation","title":"Negation","text":["Put non before the verb. Double negatives are normal: non ho niente.","Put non before the verb. Italian uses double negatives: non ho niente (I do not have anything)."],"rows":[["not","non + verb","nohn"],["nothing","niente","NYEHN-teh"],["nobody","nessuno","nehs-SOO-noh"],["never","mai","my"],["non + verb","non parlo","non PAR-loh"],["nothing","niente / nulla","nee-EHN-teh / NOOL-lah"],["nobody","nessuno","nehs-SOO-noh"],["never","mai","mah-ee"]],"ex":[["I want","voglio","VOH-lyoh"],["I do not want","non voglio","non VOH-lyoh"],["I speak English","parlo inglese","PAR-loh een-GLEH-zeh"],["I do not speak English","non parlo inglese","non PAR-loh een-GLEH-zeh"],["I like it","mi piace","mee pee-AH-cheh"],["I do not like it","non mi piace","non mee pee-AH-cheh"],["she is here","lei è qui","lay eh kwee"],["she is not here","lei non è qui","lay non eh kwee"],["I have a car","ho la macchina","oh lah MAHK-kee-nah"],["I do not have a car","non ho la macchina","non oh lah MAHK-kee-nah"],["I understand","capisco","kah-PEE-skoh"],["I do not understand","non capisco","non kah-PEE-skoh"],["we are tired","siamo stanchi","see-AH-moh STAHN-kee"],["we are not tired","non siamo stanchi","non see-AH-moh STAHN-kee"],["he works on Sundays","lavora la domenica","lah-VOH-rah lah doh-MEH-nee-kah"],["he does not work on Sundays","non lavora la domenica","non lah-VOH-rah lah doh-MEH-nee-kah"]]},{"id":"asking-questions","title":"Asking questions","text":["Yes or no question: same words as a statement, with a rising voice and a question mark. Or add \"vero?\" (right?)."],"rows":[["statement","Parli inglese.","PAR-lee een-GLEH-zeh"],["question","Parli inglese?","PAR-lee een-GLEH-zeh"],["add \"right?\"","vero?","VEH-roh"]],"ex":[["do you speak English?","parli inglese?","PAR-lee een-GLEH-zeh"],["is she a doctor?","è un medico?","eh oon MEH-dee-koh"],["do you have a pen?","hai una penna?","eye OO-nah PEHN-nah"],["are you tired?","sei stanco?","say STAHN-koh"],["is it far?","è lontano?","eh lohn-TAH-noh"]]},{"id":"question-words","title":"Question words","text":[],"rows":[["what","che cosa / cosa","keh KOH-zah"],["who","chi","kee"],["where","dove","DOH-veh"],["when","quando","KWAHN-doh"],["why","perché","pair-KEH"],["how","come","KOH-meh"],["which","quale","KWAH-leh"],["how much / how many","quanto / quanti","KWAHN-toh / KWAHN-tee"]],"ex":[["what is this?","che cos'è?","keh koh-ZEH"],["who is she?","chi è lei?","kee eh lay"],["where do you live?","dove abiti?","DOH-veh AH-bee-tee"],["when is the exam?","quando è l'esame?","KWAHN-doh eh leh-ZAH-meh"],["why are you late?","perché sei in ritardo?","pair-KEH say een ree-TAR-doh"],["how much is it?","quanto costa?","KWAHN-toh KOH-stah"]]},{"id":"possessives","title":"Possessives","text":[],"rows":[["my","il mio / la mia","eel MEE-oh / lah MEE-ah"],["your (informal)","il tuo / la tua","eel TOO-oh / lah TOO-ah"],["his / her","il suo / la sua","eel SOO-oh / lah SOO-ah"],["our","il nostro","eel NOH-stroh"],["your (plural)","il vostro","eel VOH-stroh"],["their","il loro","eel LOH-roh"]],"ex":[["my house","la mia casa","lah MEE-ah KAH-zah"],["your friends","i tuoi amici","ee TWOY ah-MEE-chee"],["his sister","sua sorella","SOO-ah soh-REHL-lah"],["our teacher","il nostro insegnante","eel NOH-stroh een-sehn-YAHN-teh"],["my mother","mia madre","MEE-ah MAH-dreh"]]},{"id":"formal-vs-informal","title":"Formal vs informal","text":["tu / tuo for friends. Lei / suo for strangers. Lei is not \"she\" here: it is the polite you, and the verb is in the he / she form."],"rows":[["you, informal","tu","too"],["you, formal","Lei","lay"],["your, informal","tuo / tua","TOO-oh / TOO-ah"],["your, formal","suo / sua","SOO-oh / SOO-ah"]],"ex":[["you speak (informal)","tu parli","too PAR-lee"],["you speak (formal)","Lei parla","lay PAR-lah"],["how are you? (informal)","come stai?","KOH-meh sty"],["how are you? (formal)","come sta?","KOH-meh stah"],["thank you, sir","grazie, signore","GRAHT-see-eh seen-YOH-reh"]]},{"id":"past-and-future-simple","title":"Past and future (simple)","text":["Past: avere (or essere) + past participle: ho parlato, sono andato. Future: infinitive + -ò, -ai, -à, -emo, -ete, -anno."],"rows":[["I spoke","ho parlato","oh par-LAH-toh"],["I ate","ho mangiato","oh mahn-JAH-toh"],["I went","sono andato","SOH-noh ahn-DAH-toh"],["I will speak","parlerò","par-leh-ROH"]],"ex":[["yesterday I worked","ieri ho lavorato","YEH-ree oh lah-voh-RAH-toh"],["she bought a book","ha comprato un libro","ah kohm-PRAH-toh oon LEE-broh"],["I went home","sono tornato a casa","SOH-noh tor-NAH-toh ah KAH-zah"],["I will call you tomorrow","ti chiamerò domani","tee kyah-meh-ROH doh-MAH-nee"],["we will eat at eight","mangeremo alle otto","mahn-jeh-REH-moh AHL-leh OT-toh"]]},{"id":"commands","title":"Commands","text":["Informal (tu): -are verbs end in -a (parla), -ere / -ire verbs in -i (scrivi). Negative tu: non + infinitive (non parlare). Formal (Lei): parli, scriva."],"rows":[["speak! (informal)","parla!","PAR-lah"],["do not speak!","non parlare!","non par-LAH-reh"],["speak! (formal)","parli!","PAR-lee"]],"ex":[["come here","vieni qui","vee-EH-nee kwee"],["do not come here","non venire qui","non veh-NEE-reh kwee"],["sit down","siediti","see-EH-dee-tee"],["do not sit down","non sederti","non seh-DEHR-tee"],["be quiet","stai zitto","STAH-ee TSEET-toh"],["do not be late","non fare tardi","non FAH-reh TAR-dee"],["open the door","apri la porta","AH-pree lah POR-tah"],["close the window","chiudi la finestra","kee-OO-dee lah fee-NEH-strah"],["listen to me","ascoltami","ah-SKOL-tah-mee"],["do not worry","non ti preoccupare","non tee preh-ok-koo-PAH-reh"],["speak slowly","parla lentamente","PAR-lah lehn-tah-MEHN-teh"],["wait a moment","aspetta un momento","ah-SPEHT-tah oon moh-MEHN-toh"]]},{"id":"can-must-want","title":"Can, must, want","text":["potere (can), dovere (must), volere (want) + infinitive: posso nuotare, devo andare, voglio mangiare."],"rows":[["I can","posso","POHS-soh"],["I must","devo","DEH-voh"],["I want","voglio","VOH-lyoh"]],"ex":[["I can swim","so nuotare","soh nwoh-TAH-reh"],["I cannot swim","non so nuotare","non soh nwoh-TAH-reh"],["can you help me?","puoi aiutarmi?","PWOH-ee ah-ee-oo-TAR-mee"],["we must go","dobbiamo andare","dob-bee-AH-moh ahn-DAH-reh"],["we must not go","non dobbiamo andare","non dob-bee-AH-moh ahn-DAH-reh"],["I want to eat","voglio mangiare","VOH-lyoh mahn-JAH-reh"],["I do not want to eat","non voglio mangiare","non VOH-lyoh mahn-JAH-reh"],["you can come","puoi venire","PWOH-ee veh-NEE-reh"],["you cannot come","non puoi venire","non PWOH-ee veh-NEE-reh"],["she wants to study","lei vuole studiare","lay VWOH-leh stoo-dee-AH-reh"],["I must work today","devo lavorare oggi","DEH-voh lah-voh-RAH-reh OHD-jee"],["you must not run","non devi correre","non DEH-vee KOR-reh-reh"]]},{"id":"in-on-at","title":"In, on, at","text":["in = in; su = on; a = at / to; sotto = under; accanto a = next to; vicino a = near; alle nove = at nine."],"rows":[["on","su","soo"],["under","sotto","SOHT-toh"],["next to","accanto a","ahk-KAHN-toh ah"],["near","vicino a","vee-CHEE-noh ah"]],"ex":[["the book is on the table","il libro è sul tavolo","eel LEE-broh eh sool TAH-voh-loh"],["the cat is under the table","il gatto è sotto il tavolo","eel GAHT-toh eh SOHT-toh eel TAH-voh-loh"],["I am at school","sono a scuola","SOH-noh ah SKWOH-lah"],["I am at home","sono a casa","SOH-noh ah KAH-zah"],["the shop is next to the bank","il negozio è accanto alla banca","eel neh-GOH-tsee-oh eh ahk-KAHN-toh AHL-lah BAHN-kah"],["the park is near the station","il parco è vicino alla stazione","eel PAR-koh eh vee-CHEE-noh AHL-lah stah-tsee-OH-neh"],["we meet in the morning","ci vediamo la mattina","chee veh-dee-AH-moh lah maht-TEE-nah"],["the lesson is at nine","la lezione è alle nove","lah leh-tsee-OH-neh eh AHL-leh NOH-veh"],["the key is in the bag","la chiave è nella borsa","lah kee-AH-veh eh NEHL-lah BOR-sah"]]},{"id":"comparing-things","title":"Comparing things","text":["più + adjective + di / che = more than (più grande di me). meno... di = less than. il più... = the most. migliore = better, peggiore = worse."],"rows":[["bigger than","più grande di","pyoo GRAHN-deh dee"],["better","meglio / migliore","MEH-lyoh / mee-LYOH-reh"],["the biggest","il più grande","eel pyoo GRAHN-deh"]],"ex":[["big, bigger, the biggest","grande, più grande, il più grande","GRAHN-deh pyoo GRAHN-deh eel pyoo GRAHN-deh"],["small, smaller, the smallest","piccolo, più piccolo, il più piccolo","PEEK-koh-loh pyoo PEEK-koh-loh eel pyoo PEEK-koh-loh"],["this is better than that","questo è meglio di quello","KWEH-stoh eh MEH-lyoh dee KWEHL-loh"],["this is worse than that","questo è peggio di quello","KWEH-stoh eh PEHD-joh dee KWEHL-loh"],["she is taller than me","lei è più alta di me","lay eh pyoo AHL-tah dee meh"],["Tashkent is bigger than Samarkand","Tashkent è più grande di Samarcanda","tahsh-KEHNT eh pyoo GRAHN-deh dee sah-mar-KAHN-dah"],["it is the cheapest","è il più economico","eh eel pyoo eh-koh-NOH-mee-koh"],["the same as","uguale a","oo-GWAH-leh ah"]]},{"id":"everyday-sentences","title":"Everyday sentences","text":["Extra practice with the most useful patterns."],"rows":[],"ex":[["he is a teacher","lui è un insegnante","LOO-ee eh oon een-seh-NYAHN-teh"],["you (plural) are students","voi siete studenti","VOH-ee see-EH-teh stoo-DEHN-tee"],["I am happy","sono felice","SOH-noh feh-LEE-cheh"],["she is at school","lei è a scuola","lay eh ah SKWOH-lah"],["you are my friend","sei il mio amico","say eel MEE-oh ah-MEE-koh"],["it is cold","fa freddo","fah FREHD-doh"],["I study English","studio inglese","STOO-dee-oh een-GLEH-zeh"],["he teaches maths","insegna matematica","een-SEH-nyah mah-teh-MAH-tee-kah"],["they work every day","lavorano ogni giorno","lah-voh-RAH-noh OH-nyee JOR-noh"],["is this your book?","è questo il tuo libro?","eh KWEH-stoh eel TOO-oh LEE-broh"],["are they here?","sono qui?","SOH-noh kwee"],["do you like tea?","ti piace il tè?","tee pee-AH-cheh eel teh"],["what time is it?","che ora è?","keh OH-rah eh"],["whose book is this?","di chi è questo libro?","dee kee eh KWEH-stoh LEE-broh"],["how old are you?","quanti anni hai?","KWAHN-tee AHN-nee AH-ee"],["how do you say it?","come si dice?","KOH-meh see DEE-cheh"],["your book (formal)","il suo libro","eel SOO-oh LEE-broh"],["their house","la loro casa","lah LOH-roh KAH-zah"],["my phone","il mio telefono","eel MEE-oh teh-LEH-foh-noh"],["excuse me, sir","mi scusi, signore","mee SKOO-zee seen-YOH-reh"],["please sit down (formal)","si accomodi, prego","see ahk-KOH-moh-dee PREH-goh"],["come here (informal)","vieni qui","vee-EH-nee kwee"],["yesterday I was tired","ieri ero stanco","ee-EH-ree EH-roh STAHN-koh"],["I will study tomorrow","studierò domani","stoo-dee-eh-ROH doh-MAH-nee"],["we went to the park","siamo andati al parco","see-AH-moh ahn-DAH-tee ahl PAR-koh"]]}],"name":"Italian","id":"it","flag":"it","note":""}